{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament\/youngII"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament\/youngii"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Young II (Thomas Young, 1800).","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"youngII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Six consecutive fifths from C to F♯ — C→G, G→D, D→A, A→E, E→B, B→F♯ — are each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"narrowed by ⅙ of the Pythagorean comma, equal to 2^(13\/6)\/3 ≈ 698.045 cents.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"The remaining six fifths are pure (3:2). The circle closes exactly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The tempered fifth size is identical to Vallotti, but the tempered segment runs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from C through F♯ (six sharps) rather than from F through B (six naturals\/flats).","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Published in "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"Philosophical Transactions of the Royal Society","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" 90 (1800)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:10IvorTuning0B6SystemPA2A15WellTemperamentVRszrlE7youngIIAEvpZ::SYNTHESIZED::s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","modules":[{"name":"IvorTuning"}],"title":"youngII","extendedModule":"IvorTuning","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"youngII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV"}],"conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Self","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"WellTemperament","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}]},"symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Type Property","role":"symbol"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"WellTemperament"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament","abstract":[{"text":"A tuning system in which all twelve keys are usable but have distinct tonal characters,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"achieved by distributing the Pythagorean comma unevenly around the circle of fifths.","type":"text"}],"title":"WellTemperament","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"WellTemperament"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Musical pitch, interval, and tuning system types."}],"title":"IvorTuning","role":"collection","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ivor